{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791842002,"nonce":"/j1xsFxTBeEnqA9cN13fNkaiesw=","message":"Rollout committed on local main: 384b753cf09a2c3c4a0422a2c1ed96ffe7bab55b (ash: enable bounded standalone tree fusion by default).\n\nStandalone execution now establishes the existing guarded allocation-elision contract by default. --no-tree-fusion disables it; --tree-fusion-log or --jit-log reports candidates/refusals/helper size/budgets. The legacy --dev-tree-fusion option still requires the contract. Unsupported runtime contracts fall back to original bytecode. Export/AOT/wasm and hot-reload paths retain original bytecode; the read-only survey bypasses default fusion.\n\nCost bounds: at most 4096 functions examined, 256 raw ops/2048 registers per caller, cheap recursive-object return filter before AIR lowering, 128 surveys at 16384 steps/64 sites each, 8 MiB retained caller AIR. Existing helper limits remain 32 helpers, 2048 ops per helper, 16384 total helper ops and 16 MiB helper AIR. Unknown/over-budget callers stay original; retained AIR/helper overflow aborts the transaction. No-candidate/fallback preparation borrows the original module without copying metadata. Lowered-body caches are temporary and capped at 2 MiB.\n\nValidation: five core tree-fusion tests (including actual host policy refusal, budget fallback, atomicity/serialization and no-candidate ownership), 16 LLVM-enabled CLI tests, 11 no-LLVM CLI tests, and 14 Python harness tests passed. LLVM-enabled survey test was rerun after the diagnostic bypass change. YAML parsing and git diff --check passed. Default debug and release binaries rebuilt.\n\nBroader local release screen: Apple M1 Pro, same executable, seven alternating default/off pairs after warmup, two separate phase/cache/RSS diagnostic pairs on each of fib, fib_calls, full Mandelbrot, DeltaBlue, arrays, SIMD, dynamic dispatch, and the refusal/startup fixture. All outputs